I thought "supportable" came down to the power usage of the drives.  The
"one drive" limit dates back to the RD52 days, and an RD52 is a really
hungry drive.  Even so, I had a VSII running with an RD53 and an RD52,
an outboard TK50 and a few other bits, and still had it within spec.  

The systems & options catalogues have a configuration worksheet that you
can use to work out whether your configuration will be within spec or not.

