In article <CJxA0p.3GL@lincoln.gpsemi.com>, dsc@pepper.swindon.gpsemi.com 
(Dave Clarke x8048) writes:
|>	I've just got a VAXstation II but no keyboard/mouse/monitor.
|>	What I would like to know is can I easily add an external terminal to the
|>9 pin port in the rear and use that, I do have a BCC08 console cable if that is
|>needed. Are their any other major differences between a UVAX II and the
|>VAXstation apart from the two VAXstation graphics boards ?

You can use the BCC08 to connect a terminal to the printer port.  You may
want to remove the graphics adapter card (and make sure that you insert
bus grant cards or move the others up so that no slots are empty).

|>	Also, what do the picture symbols mean against the switch at the back of
|>the VAXstation, not the baud rate selector switch the other one.

There are two other switches.  The toggle switch is the Halt Enable/Disable
switch.  In the up position (circle with dot inside), this is Halt Enable;
this causes the system to enter console mode on power-up (or any other halt
condition) and also enables BREAK on the printer port to switch to console
mode (^P may do this too).  If the switch is down (dot outside circle), the
system will ignore BREAK from the printer port and will reboot on power-up.

The three-position dial is the Mode switch.  The upper position with the
arrow is the normal run position.  The middle position is for language
inquiry (for systems equipped for multi-language console) and I don't know
what the T-in-a-circle position is for.  The manuals I have for the VSII are
not very helpful about these switches.

The processor itself is just a normal MicroVAX II.
