The DECUS U.S. Chapter has issued a Call for Participation for the
Spring 1994 National Event being held in New Orleans, LA, May 9-12,
1994.  The deadline for submitting a session is Tuesday, February 1st.

You can get a copy of the complete CFP and information about the
format and focus of the event via anonymous ftp to decus.org in file
[.decus94-neworleans]cfp.txt, via mail server by sending one-line
message SEND [DECUS94-NEWORLEANS]CFP.TXT to mailserv@decus.org, or by
calling 1-800-DECUS55.

The focus of DECUS '94/New Orleans is "Managing Complexity: Succeeding
in a Multivendor, Multiplatform World."  This is something almost all
of us with OpenVMS systems do every day.  We are very interested in
sessions that deal with your experiences, particularly in your use of
VMS systems as servers in your enterprise's client/server or trans-
action processing environment.

In addition, we encourage novice, intermediate and advanced (except
where noted) sessions on the following topics:

  o OpenVMS VAX to OpenVMS AXP migration experiences
  o VMS internals and systems programming
  o VMS system and resource management
  o VMS system tuning and performance management
  o RMS tuning
  o VMS POSIX
  o VMSclusters
  o novice use of VMS and DCL

To submit an OpenVMS session, you should obtain the CFP form, complete
it, and then e-mail it to information@decus.org, fax it to 508-841-3357,
or postal mail it to the address listed on the form.

We look forward to your submission.  Remember, the deadline is
February 1st!

