On a vt420 terminal, you can redefine the character sent by the <x] key
(called "Backarrow key" in the vt420 manual) using the Set-Up Screen
or by sending the following keyboard control sequence:

Backspace:	CSI ? 67 h  
DEL (default):	CSI ? 67 l

(CSI is ESC [).

Is it possible to redefine the Backarrow key on on a DECstation
5000/xxx console in a similar way ??

The machines in question is runing ULTRIX 4.3.

I know that the backarrow key can be redefined in a DECterm using the
options menu General, but that only affects the this application. I
want the change to affect not only X-applications but also
character-based applications using e.g. the termio interface (which
means that xmodmap cannot be used).

The redefinition method should also work when the machine is runing in
non-graphics mode (before starting the X-server) e.g. in single-user mode.

Jens Bloch Nielsen (jbn@stl.dk)


