Jarkko Torppa (torppa@mits.mdata.fi) wrote:

: I got a DECstation 2100 without monitor/mouse and keyboard. I would
: like to know if there is way to run that machine headless, using RS
: port as console.

  I think that this is covered in the ultrix-faq on gatekeeper, but 
yes. Check to see if the VSIMM is installed in the CPU module (you'll
need to open the box, the VSIMM is an oversized SIMM just past the end
of the memory SIMMs). If you remove the VSIMM from its socket, the
DECstation diagnostics will believe that the system is a DECsystem and
not a DECstation. I believe that the default console port is tty00, but
that's from memory.

: Would it be possible to use the old mouse from VAXstation2000 with
: that machine ?

  I believe that mouse is the VSXXX-AA or VSXXX-AB. If my memory serves
me correctly, either of those two mice should work on the DECstation.

: Otherwise it would be nice to have pinouts for the monitor port so
: that i could test that machine.

  Sorry, I don't happen to have the pin-outs. But, you can find the
DS2100/DS3100 functional specification up on gatekeeper, and the pin
out may be there.

