  Previously I distributed a preliminary announcement about Supercomputing
Symposium '94 (SS'94), the Canadian high performance computing conference
and exhibition to be held in Toronto on June 6-8. This time I am sending
you the official Call For Papers. The CFP has been distributed using several
mechanisms; I apologize if you have received more than one copy. Information
about conference registration will be generally available in early February.
  Dr. Edmund West (Chairman, SS'94)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

                       CALL FOR PAPERS

            Supercomputing Symposium '94 (SS'94)

      Canada's Eighth Annual High Performance Computing
                  Conference and Exhibition

                       June 6--8, 1994
                   Toronto, Ontario Canada

             Sponsored by: Supercomputing Canada
              Hosted by: University of Toronto


______TOPICS
The symposium is concerned with all aspects of high performance
computing. It attempts to expose attendees to the latest developments
in this field. Papers are sought that describe the hardware, software,
programming tools and techniques, applications and experiences related
to high performance computing.

Topics of interest include, but are not limited to:
  o vector computing technology
  o parallel computing technology
  o workstation clusters
  o parallel programming techniques
  o distributed computing
  o languages for high performance computing
  o experiences with high performance computers
  o applications of high performance computing technology to
    solve problems in government, academia and industry
  o networking and communications
  o scientific data visualization
  o compiler and operating system issues

You are also invited to submit proposals for tutorials, panel
discussions, debates, demonstrations or other specialized sessions
that address any aspect of high performance computing.


___________SUBMISSIONS
Contributors are invited to send a detailed abstract or proposal
including the information specified below to the Program Chairman.

Upon notification of acceptance, you will be sent an author's
guideline and required to submit your final paper in hardcopy or
electronic form. It is not necessary to submit a paper if you do not
wish it to appear in the conference proceedings.

Note that all authors and speakers will be required to pay for their
registration by the final paper submission deadline; otherwise the
papers will not be included in the proceedings and the talk will not
be scheduled. Submissions will not be refereed, but in order to have
as broad a participation as possible from researchers while keeping
the number of papers to a reasonable level, we may restrict the number
of papers to one per author. If this will present a problem please
contact the Program Chair before submitting your abstract.

Please send submissions by post or e-mail to:

