>I'm looking for some example of SCSI_CAM routines usage.
>I would like to use an existing driver to submit a generic command
>to a certain SCSI device.
>I would like avoid writing a new driver even using  the low level 
>SCSI CAM routines.

    If you are interested in sending down SCSI commands to a SCSI device
you do not have to write or port a kernel driver.  The CAM subsystem
comes with a User Agent, (UAgt - /dev/cam), driver that will allow 
a user level application to issue CAM CCBs to devices.  The CCB
structure is the same and you pass the command(s) via an ioctl() call.

>I need it for AXP/OSF but probably MIPS/Ultrix is very similar.

	The CAM subsystem is supported on both, and from a peripheral
device driver or user app. the differences are minimal.

