According to the Alpha Architecture Ref. manual, a call_pal
instruction involves stalling "instruction issue until all prior
instructions are guaranteed to complete without incurring exceptions"
followed by a trap into PALcode.

What I would like to know is how many cycles it typically takes to
switch into PALmode and back into normal mode.  For example, has
anybody data available on how long a no-operation PAL instruction
would take?  I think the OSF/1 "read processor status" (rdps) pal
instruction could serve as a reasonable approximation for this as it
presumably does nothing but read a processor internal register.
Unfortunately, it is a privileged instruction so I don't see an easy
way to measure this without access to source for an Alpha operating
system.

Any help would be greatly appreciated.

