According to some earlier measurements with an internal PALcode monitor,
I show 36.9 average cycles to do a RDPS call.

I don't have the PALcode listings handy, but I seem to recall that a
RDPS just does a MFPR, which should be a two-cycle operation.


There are a few calls that complete faster (on average), typically
other MFPR's. I suspect the differences are due to the statistical
differences in context when they are called.


