Note 377.0                    The death of Phase IV                   79 replies
EISNER::HOLDREGE "Matt Holdrege - 486.83"            27 lines   9-DEC-1993 20:36
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    I've been hearing a lot of talk about DEC removing Phase IV DECNET from
    VMS 6.2. I decided to do some serious investigation while attending
    DECUS. 
    
    Everyone had a different story, so I kept climbing to the top for the
    definitive answer. I got to Chris Lehmkule, who is the business manager
    for DECNET. She is responsible for the $200 million budget for
    development and maintenance of DECNET. 
    
    Chris said that DECNET Phase IV ends with VMS 6.1. Period, end of
    story, don't listen to anyone else. When you upgrade to VMS 6.2, you
    will use Phase V or you won't use DECNET at all.
    
    Her explanation is that she must concentrate DEC's efforts on one or
    the other, and Phase IV is obsolete. Each new version of VMS requires
    major rewriting of DECNET and she can't commit those resources for
    Phase IV anymore.
    
    I brought up the issue to many people here that Phase V brings zero
    benefit to me and most other DEC customers. Similar to converting to
    AXP, much effort is required for large shops. Unlike the conversion to
    AXP, we will gain nothing for all our efforts. 
    
    Chris said that the only way that we will get Phase IV beyond VMS 6.1,
    would be to get a VP to overrule her. She said that would be very
    unlikely.


