   write-protect that is set when the floppy tab is set a certain way?  i.e.
   if I write protect a floppy, is there *any* way for the floppy to be
   written?

As far as I know, write-protect tabs on floppies, tapes, etc, are enforced by
the drive's hardware, and cannot be overridden by software. One of the reasons
they're tabs you have to close is a fail-safe design: If the <whatever>
illuminating the hole dies (the most likely failure mode), is just as if the
thing was write-protected.

	Jan


