>
>
>I've some program on VAX/VMS that use the generic SCSI Drive (GKDRIVER)
>Now I Want to port themto Alpha OSF. Is there something available on
>Alpha OSF.
>
>What I really need is the possibility to write a generic SCSI command
>to a certain SCSI address.

    The SCSI/CAM sub-system in OSF contains what we call the User Agent,
UAgt, and it can be accessed via /dev/cam.  The uagt.h and cam.h include
files in /usr/sys/include/io/cam should give you a rough idea of what the
data structures look like.

    The task of creating/running a GKDRIVER and UAgt application is not 
difficult.  In fact the first CAM program we had running was a scanner
program that was able to translate scanner stuff into the two protocols.

