|>Why does it work on an OpenVMS AXP system, but fails on a VAXstation?
|>

That fwrite call tells VAX C to write 100 records that are each
4 bytes long.  The fopen statement says to create a file where
every record is a fixed length, and that length is 512.  RMS
complains because it expects 512 and it is only given 4 at a time.

Try mrs=4 if you want 4 byte records, or mrs=400 and 1 item of 400
bytes (the size of the whole array) for the fwrite().

DEC C works a little differently.  It interprets the fwrite call
as a desire to write 400 bytes, using as many records as necessary.

I used fopen mode "wb" since the program is writing binary data.

