>the Alpha dissipates more than 30 watts at 200 MHz and 3.3 volts :)

A working prototype with over 2 hours of battery life was shown at Comdex in 
November. Just because a chip can run at 200 MHz and at 3.3V, it does not have 
to be used that that frequency or voltage in a laptop. 

Power = Capacitance * (voltage**2) * frequency

By lowering both voltage and frequency, significant power reduction can be 
obtained. The prototype was based on a 21066 running at 25-125 MHz at lower
voltage.

