There  is a  lesson  in this  for  would be UNIX  purchasers.  As no two
vendors  ship the exact same UNIX,  before  you start  your  development
project,  you should pick some  programming  standards  to keep you from
getting  stuck.  It may  even be  possible  that by  picking  the  right
standards  you can  run  your  application  on both  UNIX  and  non-UNIX
systems.  An open  OS does  not  equal  a  portable  application  if the
application is written using lots vendor specific "enhancements".

