|> Get to be an 11/780 - lots of boards in the CPU...

It should be obvious that the terms 'microcomputer', 'minicomputer' and
'mainframe' are comparative terms such as 'small', 'medium' and 'large'.

Everyone has their own perception of how various computers fit into these
categories.  As technology develops, your criteria (CPU power, number of
boards, physical size/weight, I/O power, etc) WILL be invalidated and
you WILL become as disoriented to these terms as the next person.  It would
perhaps be better to categorize computers based on the relative speeds
of their various bus structures - admittedly complicated by several
busses on some machines...

