My situation exactly. Did you change /usr/lib/X11/xdm/Xsession to run
your window manager?  Mine is enclosed at the end; note the trick with
( ) wait, to prevent creation of zombies. Other than that, xdm should
create the initial ~/.Xauthority file, and you are responsible for
propagating it to other hosts that you want to access your display
from.  Note that Ultrix 4.2 did not have MIT-COOKIE method compiled
into X libraries, so that 4.2 clients could not access server running
this authorization method. VMS is plain out of the question, although
I do manage to open windows from VMS systems, by doing explicit
  xhost +VMSHOST (on my machine)
  running the program (on VMS)
  xhost -VMSHOST
i.e., xhost and xauth are not mutually exclusive, although Tk will check
to make sure that xhost does not allow any hosts.

