>Some questions about ULTRIX 4.3 on VAX6000 systems:
>  - How many processors will ULTRIX support?

I've used a 3 processor system and I think ultrix will support the maximum
number of cards (4? 6?).

>  - I understand ULTRIX will only support non-SMP multiprocessing,
>    meaning among other things that all I/O is handled by the first
>    CPU, the others can only do number crunching really without requiring
>    assistance from the first, this true?

Other than interrupts, the kernel is SMP.  The device drivers are mostly
(all?) SMP code but kernel statistics show all interrupts handled by the
boot CPU.

>Any other general observations/quirks/etc with regard to using multiprocessor
>VAX6000 systems to run ULTRIX?

With enough memory and processors you can get good performance.  On parallel
jobs (for example, large compiles with a multiprocessing make) performance
with 3 CPUs is very close to 3 times performance with 1 CPU.

Unfortunately Ultrix is not supported on the high end model, the 6000-600.


