This is on a DEC 3000/300 running:
   DEC OSF/1 V1.3 (Rev. 111); Sun Dec 12 11:31:43 CST 1993
   DEC OSF/1 V1.3 Worksystem Software (Rev. 111)

I have an application which calls mount() which I am attempting to port
from Ultrix to OSF/1 and the mount() routine is returning errno=46
     EPFNOSUPPORT ``Protocol family not supported''
which is, of course, not mentioned in the man page... :-(

The arguments to mount are:

     mount(MOUNT_NFS, "/nfs/fs-10/u4", M_NOSUID, &nfs_args);

The directory exists (ls -ldg /nfs/fs-10/u4):
drwxrwxrwx   2 root     system       512 Jan 03 00:53 /nfs/fs-10/u4

And the structure nfs_args contains:
 addr
  sin_family = 2
  sin_port   = 2049
  sin_addr   = 129.186.160.160
 fh          = 221500008003000040f29d5b8003000040f29d5b000000000000000000000000
 flags       = 0000003f
 rsize       = 4096
 wsize       = 4096
 timeo       = 8
 retrans     = 7
 hostname    = "fs-10.iastate.edu"
 acregmin    = 3
 acregmax    = 60
 acdirmin    = 30
 acdirmax    = 60
 netname     = "fs-10.iastate.edu"
 pathconf    = 14002bcf0 (pointer to zero'd struct pathcnf)
 (The server fs-10 is running Ultrix 4.2a (hence the fh format above.)

All of which look OK to me?

Any clues would be much appreciated...
(PS, I can mount this filesystem on this dir using the mount command,
but I really don't want to modify the application to fork&exec it
if I can avoid it).

