> > In article <2g5qlv$irn@ariel.ucs.unimelb.EDU.AU> dcb@mulka.ph.unimelb.edu.au (David Bell) writes:
> >>I have a Vax Station 2000 and would like to remove the console
> >>Screen from the top of the display. This appears when the system
> >>produces messages, And moves the decwindows down when visable.
> >>how to fix this problem?
> > 
> 
> 	For a more "permanent" fix, place the following in the system startup
> for the workstation (this turns off the console messages that cause the
> display to drop a 1/4 screen to display them):
>
>	$ ASSIGN OPA0: SYS$COMMAND/USER
>	$ REPLY/DISABLE

SYS$MANAGER:SYLOGICALS.(COM|TEMPLATE) contains some documentation on how to
control what goes onto the console and into the operator log files, by defining
the appropriate logical names. You can also redirect the operator logs to a
different file, on a different disk if necessary.
e.g.

	$ define/system/exec OPC$OPA0_ENABLE FALSE

will disable the console as an operator.
