When I see stuff like this I wonder, what that 130ppm printer is doing
with all that paper.  Like, No matter what kind of printer(s) you have you
have to load the input hopper(s), and collect paper from the output
stackers.  That means people.  How much more than 2000 sheets (max input
capacity on the 4si) can you cram in this behmoth. and how much output
will the stacker hold.  Do you have equipment on site to automatically
lift the output paper in a stack of 5000 sheets (1 case of paper) and
carry it to it's destination?  How long does it take to add
toner/drum/cartridges to the big laser?  I can replace a 4si cartridge
in 2 minutes or so, including the time to open the box and put the old
cartridge back in the box for refilling, and carry it to the recycle
stack.

I can't believe that a 130ppm laser requires less than half the operator
service time of 8 17ppm ones.  You still have to open boxes and unwrap
all that paper.

The only way I could see needing this kind of thruput in a single device
is in some sort of a linked enviroment where a bill/mailing comes off
the printer and directly into an envelope stuffer or something. 

>  be to purchase another high-capacity printer or two, purchase a set of fast
>  system boxes, one for each of the 4-5 printers (you may need five if its true
>  that no cheap box can drive a single one of these printers at its rated
