High volume batch operations are expensive.  What do the people who run
it do for the _rest_ of the month?  Balancing workloads in a business is
_very_ important.  What does all that expensive equipment bought to
handle a BIG peak cycle do for the rest of the month?  Spending $200K on
a piece of equipment used 2 days a month does not sound very cost
effective to me in this instance.  The amortization/depreciation cost of
this kind of equipment brings your bloody cost / sheet up to the ceiling.

Postage costs on mailing do not drop off that dramatically after about
the 5000 piece level.  My memory is sketchy here but the costs you pay
are based on the number of peices within a given 3 digit pre-sort, and
then a given 5 digit pre-sort.  It would seem busting a mailing into 3
or 5 digit pre-sort groups and processing zipcodes X->Y during a given
week would save the same postage dollar and distribute the load.  Shoot
I just wrote the code to do the sorting/printing here.

