These are the criteria I use, more or less:

A micro is a computer with the CPU on a single chip.

A mini is a computer with the CPU on a single card.

A mainframe or supercomputer has the CPU on multiple cards (in the main
frame). The distinction here is that a mainframe is oriented towards pumping
data, the supercomputer towards performing calculations.
