>Can anyone from DEC confirm/deny what's going on with this rumored
>"renaming"?  Anyone from organizations that have merged or divested 
>(causing name changes) care to relate any stories of how easy this is?

Russ Jones said he'd have more to say on the subject later, and he's the
person I wrote to when I first heard about the plan.  What I have been told
so far is that the primary intent is that systems placed on the Internet
for customer access would be in the digital.com domain, but that there 
would be no rush to move all of Digital over.  We've actually done this
sort of thing once already when we added the "enet" subdomain and the
effect on the majority of systems was nil.  As I understand it, the idea
is that dec.com and digital.com would run in parallel for a number of
years. 

As a system manager, I know that if I actually had to change what domain
QUARK reported itself as being in, it would take me less than 5 minutes to
do, and most of that would be waiting for UCX to shut down and restart.
The biggest hassle I might have is inking in changes on my business
cards (though in reality I wouldn't even have to do that.)

I was initially concerned about the change, but as I've learned more
about it, I find it's not worth worrying about.  My advice (worth every
cent) is that you shouldn't worry about this either.

