In article <ah301-050194132027@sy_j.pgh.wec.com>, ah301@yfn.ysu.edu (Jerry Sy) writes:
=I am writing a simple Vax C program to calculate time difference,
=but the RTL LIB$ functions does not seem to be returning to me
=the correct results.  can anybody tell me what I am doing wrong ?
=
=My code is shown below. I know that the difference should be 30 minutes
=but the RTL function gives me 24 minutes as the difference between
=7:30 and 7:00!
=
=please email replies if possible.
=thanks in advance
=
=JERRY
=
=
=/* INCLUDE FILES */
=#include stdio
=#include stdlib
=#include time
=#include string
=#include descrip
=#include libdtdef
=
=unsigned long	result,operation,delta_min;
=typedef struct	dsc$descriptor_s	desctype;
=desctype		dateA,dateB;
=unsigned long	qDateA,qDateB,qDateDiff;

A lonwgword is two words (32 bits);  a quadword is 4 words (64 bits [2
longwords]).  Change this declaration to:
	unsigned long	qDateA[2],qDateB[2],qDateDiff[2];
and your problem will be fixed
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
