>I have a Vax Station 2000 and would like to remove the console
>Screen from the top of the display. This appears when the system
>produces messages, And moves the decwindows down when visable.
>how to fix this problem?

Depending on how your system s/w (VMS assumed) was installed, you'd 
enter: 1.) F2 - or - 2.) Ctrl/F2. This is not a permanent solution but
just returns the VR260 (assumedd) to the display it had before the
message(s) went to the system's console. Entering the above also displays
the last several lines of messages that went to the system's console
also..  - i.e. F2 is a toggle 'switch'.

