dcb@mulka.ph.unimelb.edu.au (David Bell) writes...
>I have a Vax Station 2000 and would like to remove the colsole
>Screen from the top of the display. This appears when the system
>produces messages, And moves the decwindows down when visable.
>how to fix this problem?

Pete Cull already told you how to restore the screen when this happens.
Now I'll tell you how to prevent it from happening again, if you indeed
want that.

First, in SYS$MANAGER:SYLOGICALS.COM, add the line:

	$ DEFINE/SYSTEM OPC$OPA0_ENABLE FALSE

This will disable the workstation console window from being an operator
terminal and will prevent most console broadcast messages from appearing
there.  However, mount-verify messages will still appear; to disable
those, add the following line to your system startup procedure:

	$ SET TERMINAL/PERMANENT/NOBROADCAST OPA0:

