In article <2furkj$rq7@quabbin.crl.dec.com> jg@crl.dec.com (Jim Gettys) writes:
>I do happen to know that  the Genroco IPI TURBOstor controller has 
>been clocked at above 30 MB/second file system performance with just a couple controllers on 
>a DEC3000/500, with lots of CPU cycles (and TURBOchannel) left over, so I could add controllers
>and up the performance. I don't happen to know what the top end is for the Genroco system.
>I believe we ran such a demo at DECUS. I'll try to find out more on how fast we can go
>and whether the SCSI controller is truly dual when I get back from New Years next week.

Hi Jim,

The configuration we ran at DECUS consisted of two of our IPI-242T
IPI TURBOchannel disk controllers with two Seagate Elite-3 Enhanced
IPI drives on each (Digital calls this product VELOCITOR).  Each
controller striped the two drives attached to it, and the application
striped the controllers.  The demo consisted of moving an uncompressed
video animation file (~450MB) from disk to system memory, and then from
system memory to a Kubota graphics unit.  The data rate achieved from
the disk configuration was in excess of 30MB per second.  Using this data
rate, the demo diplayed the 1280x1024 PseudoColor animation at 24 frames
per second.  The total throughput on the TURBOchannel (disk + graphics
display) was in excess of 60MB per second!  This ran on a DEC 3000/800
at DECUS, but it will also run on a DEC 3000/500.


